  "result": "Quiz 0002 is ready, with its key. The title is \"Workflows, agents and who owns the control flow\", and it has six questions on O4. The files are `quizzes/0002.json` and `keys/0002.json`.\n\n- **Format:** Four are multiple choice and two are short answers.\n- **What it covers:**\n  - the core difference, which is who decides the next step;\n  - spotting that the code owns the flow even when the model does one step;\n  - choosing which makerspace parts should be fixed workflows;\n  - why a fixed workflow costs less;\n  - what you give up by turning the booking steps into an agent.\n- **Quiz ahead of the lessons:** No lesson covers O4 yet, so the questions test the objective directly. I wrote it from my own knowledge of Anthropic's \"Building effective agents\" and did not search or re-read that source. The questions use the idea of \"who owns the control flow\", which the quiz doesn't define for you.\n- **Misconception ids:** I left the `distractors` field out of the key. None of the existing ids, M1 to M6, fit these wrong answers, and I didn't want to make up new ids.\n\nDo you want a short lesson on workflows versus agents before you take it?",
